From 3d53aa5389010be43eb96e1b989242c0161c4f0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:22:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: own asynchronous response records independently of
 senders

slim_xfer_msg() submits a stack transaction and returns without waiting
when the caller supplies a completion. The TID table currently retains
that stack pointer for a later response. Closing synchronous timeout
races does not keep an asynchronous sender frame alive.

Allocate a response record per TID and snapshot its buffer, length and
completion before publishing readiness. Retain the sender address only
for software ownership comparison; response delivery never dereferences
it. Preserve the existing serialization and separate response PM pin.
Retire records on reply, send failure and synchronous timeout.

Add explicit asynchronous cancellation for lost replies. It synchronizes
with response copy/completion, rejects duplicate active descriptors and
does not report a fabricated successful response. Document caller buffer
lifetime and the requirement to serialize cancellation with resubmission.
Close TID admission and drain records before client removal. Preserve
transaction initialization across registration and initialize NGD before
RX can start. Empty IDR allocation state is destroyed during shutdown.

Codex identified the ownership gap and generated the fix and logical
fixtures. Twenty-two exact callback/helper bodies pass 1,149 cases and
44,419 checks, after 102 failures in the pre-change ownership model;
twenty-one controls are rejected. Prior readiness, power, bookkeeping
and TX regressions pass with synthetic services. Eight ARM/ARM64 objects
build with LLVM21 W=1 and strict callback diagnostics without warnings.
Checkpatch reports one inherited IDR API deprecation for moving its
existing initializer; there are no other style diagnostics.

Late wire replies after numeric TID reuse, full RX/master/external-call
quiescence, hardware stop ordering and physical recovery remain open.
No real DMA, firmware, audio, phone or network operations are exercised.
Human review and DCO certification remain pending.

Fixes: afbdcc7c384b ("slimbus: Add messaging APIs to slimbus framework")
---
